cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "oes-coordination-lab: a synthetic toy benchmark of local disturbances versus system-wide shocks under no, private and shared regime information"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/oes-coordination-lab"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC toy model with explicit payoffs and hand-coded (not learning)
  policies. Compares no regime information, independent private noisy signals
  and one shared noisy signal on the same seeded disturbances, reporting
  coordination rate, welfare, miscoordination cost and regret with confidence
  intervals over seeds, exact expectations, and an exact unilateral-deviation
  audit of each policy profile. No operational claims.
keywords:
  - "coordination"
  - "information structure"
  - "common knowledge"
  - "game theory"
  - "synthetic benchmark"
  - "python"
